# RetDec — Composer agent rules (MASTER-UPGRADE-PLAN Part 14)

## Hard boundaries

- NEVER touch `deps/llvm/` or attempt an LLVM version bump.
- NEVER modify `deps/` except pinned URL and SHA-256 lines in `cmake/deps.cmake`.
- NEVER change a public header to make an implementation compile.
- NEVER edit files not named in the current task prompt.
- NEVER delete, disable, SKIP, DISABLED_-prefix, or loosen a test. A failing test is a finding — report it.
- NEVER invent file paths, symbols, or APIs not present in the repository.

## Verification

- Build after every C++ edit.
- On build breakage: STOP and report the first compiler/link error verbatim. Do not attempt a third repair without escalation.
- Never claim complete without pasting relevant ctest or build output.

## Task sizing

- One dependency bump per branch/commit.
- One algorithm change per commit with unchanged public headers unless explicitly scoped.
- If acceptance criteria cannot be stated in one sentence, stop and ask for a narrower scope.

## Escalation triggers (stop and report)

- Same build error survives two repair attempts.
- Proposed public header change to fix implementation.
- Any test deletion or disable proposed.
- Diff exceeds ~400 lines for a mechanical task.
- llama.cpp API symbol guesswork — read `deps/llamacpp/include/llama.h` at the pinned commit first.

## Honesty

- Say when unsure and stop.
- Do not stack changes on a broken tree.
- Do not mark tasks done without verification output.
